Spec: Settings

Purpose:
  Remember folders and advisor settings on this machine, outside the repo.

Owns:
  ./settings.rs

Must:
  The file is ~/Library/Application Support/story-maker/settings.toml on macOS.
  The file is ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/story-maker/settings.toml on Linux.
  --settings PATH replaces that location and is the file the terminal writes.
  The directory mode is 0700 and the file mode is 0600.
  Fields are advise, api_base, model, api_key, clips, photos, and out.
  For one launch, a flag wins over the environment, and the environment wins over the file.
  Environment names are STORY_MAKER_API_BASE, STORY_MAKER_MODEL, and STORY_MAKER_API_KEY.
  Saving writes the file and does not copy an environment-only key into it.

Must not:
  Call ffmpeg, ffprobe, or the network.
  Store the file inside this repo.

Scenario: blank folders
  Given the settings file has empty clips, photos, and out
  And no flag supplies them
  When the program starts
  Then the settings screen opens before any media scan

Scenario: environment key stays out of the file
  Given the settings file has an empty api_key
  And STORY_MAKER_API_KEY is set
  When the person saves settings without typing a key
  Then the file still has an empty api_key
